  Reading the table: delta is grouped minus random with identical training code. A gap
  is attributable to temporal-autocorrelation leakage only where the class had train rows
  in the grouped fold, so read delta_seen. Grouped CV can leave a class with no train
  rows (a class confined to one group is held out whole), which is a zero-day effect and
  not leakage, and those rows are excluded from the _seen columns and listed above.
  Pooled AUC concatenates scores normalized per fold with that fold's train constants.
